issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-09-16T08:23:14Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T06:21:42Z","closed_at":"2026-09-24T17:29:04Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123543","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123543.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123543.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-24T17:29:04Z"},"body":"OS files and folders dropping inside the browser window has been supported for a long time, but the original implementation based on temporary \"drop\" folders was quite hacky and broken.\r\n\r\nThis commit fixes two main issues:\r\n- Dropped folders are now copied in the temporary one respecting the original structure (instead of copying all files to the top level).\r\n- The emitted signal now only reports the files/folders that were actually dropped, not all files in the dropped folders (this is a consequence of the above).\r\n\r\nThis brings it more in line with other platforms.\r\n\r\nThe JS code has been refactored for better processing, and the temporary deletion is now delegated to the display server.\r\n\r\nThe \"persistentDrops\" hack has also been dropped in favor of a localized solution in the project manager.\r\n\r\nThis might \"break compat\" if you relied on the (purposely undocumented) \"persistentDrops\" config option, or the bug causing all files to be dropped in the root of the temporary folder.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11c55c78-265b-43d2-b747-c5bdc54b0ebe\r\n\r\nNote\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe have an opportunity in the editor, to do some more filtering on what we copy by monkey-patching the controller (e.g. excluding `.godot` and `.git` from folders, and only import folders containing a project.godot file and its subfolder).\r\n\r\nI think we should do that after/on top of #123149 (I have a tentative implementation in a separate branch).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123543/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123543/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}